#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# key_drop

#% text
# `key_drop(a, [k, ...])` gives the association `a` without the keys given; `key_drop(a, k)` without one key.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# A list of rules is read as an association; a list of associations gives the list of results.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
key_drop(assoc(a -> 1, b -> 2, c -> 3), [a, c])
#% output
#= assoc(b -> 2)

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# A list of associations:

#% cell
key_drop([assoc(a -> 1, b -> 2), assoc(a -> 3)], a)
#% output
#= [assoc(b -> 2), assoc()]

#% text
# Operator form:

#% cell
key_drop([a])(assoc(a -> 1, b -> 2))
#% output
#= assoc(b -> 2)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `key_take`, `delete_key`, `keys`
